          "lineHeight": 1.4,
          "indent": 0,
          "inlines": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "text": "Two cards are drawn from a standard deck of 52 cards, ",
              "marks": []
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "text": "without",
              "marks": [
                "italic"
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "text": " replacement. What is the probability that the two cards satisfy the following?",
              "marks": []
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    "layout": "grid",
    "columns": 2,
    "questionDiagrams": [],
    "children": [
      {
        "id": "p24-q11-a",
        "type": "part",
        "label": "a",
        "prompt": "Have the same colour.",
        "layout": "list",
        "columns": null,
        "questionDiagrams": [],
        "children": [],
        "answer": {
          "short": "$\\frac{25}{51}$",
          "worked": "The matching cases are two red cards or two black cards. After one card is drawn, 25 cards of its colour remain among 51 cards.\n$$\\begin{align*}P(\\text{same colour})&=P(RR)+P(BB)\\\\P(\\text{same colour})&=\\frac{26}{52}\\times\\frac{25}{51}+\\frac{26}{52}\\times\\frac{25}{51}\\\\P(\\text{same colour})&=\\frac{25}{51}\\end{align*}$$",
          "solutionDiagrams": []
        },
        "answerSpaceMm": 70
      },
      {
        "id": "p24-q11-b",
        "type": "part",
        "label": "b",
        "prompt": "Have the same suit.",
        "layout": "list",
        "columns": null,
        "questionDiagrams": [],
        "children": [],
        "answer": {
          "short": "$\\frac{4}{17}$",
          "worked": "There are four possible matching suits. For each suit, 13 cards are available initially and 12 remain after the first draw.\n$$\\begin{align*}P(\\text{same suit})&=4\\times\\frac{13}{52}\\times\\frac{12}{51}\\\\P(\\text{same suit})&=\\frac{4}{17}\\end{align*}$$",
          "solutionDiagrams": []
        },
        "answerSpaceMm": 54
      },
      {
        "id": "p24-q11-c",
        "type": "part",
        "label": "c",
        "prompt": "Have the same rank (including A, J, Q and K).",
        "layout": "list",
        "columns": null,
        "questionDiagrams": [],
        "children": [],
        "answer": {
          "short": "$\\frac{1}{17}$",
          "worked": "There are 13 possible matching ranks. Each rank has four cards initially and three remaining after the first draw.\n$$\\begin{align*}P(\\text{same rank})&=13\\times\\frac{4}{52}\\times\\frac{3}{51}\\\\P(\\text{same rank})&=\\frac{1}{17}\\end{align*}$$",
          "solutionDiagrams": []
        },
        "answerSpaceMm": 54
      },
      {
        "id": "p24-q11-d",
        "type": "part",
        "label": "d",
        "prompt": "Are face cards (J, Q, K).",
        "layout": "list",
        "columns": null,
        "questionDiagrams": [],
        "children": [],
        "answer": {
          "short": "$\\frac{11}{221}$",
          "worked": "There are 12 face cards initially. After a face card is drawn, 11 face cards remain among 51 cards.\n$$\\begin{align*}P(\\text{both face cards})&=\\frac{12}{52}\\times\\frac{11}{51}\\\\P(\\text{both face cards})&=\\frac{11}{221}\\end{align*}$$",
          "solutionDiagrams": []
        },
        "answerSpaceMm": 46
      },
      {
        "id": "p24-q11-e",
        "type": "part",
        "label": "e",
        "prompt": "Are different colours.",
        "layout": "list",
        "columns": null,
        "questionDiagrams": [],
        "children": [],
        "answer": {
          "short": "$\\frac{26}{51}$",
          "worked": "Different colours is the complement of the event in part a.\n$$\\begin{align*}P(\\text{different colours})&=1-P(\\text{same colour})\\\\P(\\text{different colours})&=1-\\frac{25}{51}\\\\P(\\text{different colours})&=\\frac{26}{51}\\end{align*}$$",
          "solutionDiagrams": []
        },
        "answerSpaceMm": 54
      },
      {
        "id": "p24-q11-f",
        "type": "part",
        "label": "f",
        "prompt": "Are different suits.",
        "layout": "list",
        "columns": null,
        "questionDiagrams": [],
        "children": [],
        "answer": {
          "short": "$\\frac{13}{17}$",
          "worked": "Different suits is the complement of the event in part b.\n$$\\begin{align*}P(\\text{different suits})&=1-P(\\text{same suit})\\\\P(\\text{different suits})&=1-\\frac{4}{17}\\\\P(\\text{different suits})&=\\frac{13}{17}\\end{align*}$$",
          "solutionDiagrams": []
        },
        "answerSpaceMm": 46
      }
    ]
  },
